If I'm not mistaken, Jerin's reference to RP 2/3 is regarding the commonly used "Response Probability" in standard setting (Bookmark method usually) to refer to the point at which an examinee theoretically has a 2 in 3 chance of answering correctly. This would not be accomplished by using the normal ogive conversion of 1.7 (or 1.702, http://demonstrations.wolfram.com/ComparingTheNormalOgiveAndLogisticItemCharacteristicCurves/). I don't have a ready link for something with a guessing parameter, but here's how to do the adjustment within a Rasch framework: http://raschforum.boards.net/thread/87/generating-rp67-winsteps

